<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44646" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔοσμος</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔοδμος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀδμή, ὀσμή</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sweet-smelling, fragrant</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔοδμον ἔαρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					75.15
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐόδμοισι προσθετοῖσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Loc.Hom.</u>
					47
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔοσμον μύρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Achae.
					17
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ba.</u>
				235
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐόδμοισι σελίνοις, νέκταρος
				εὐόδμοιο</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				3.23
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				17.29
			</span></i>; 
				v.l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐώδης</span>
			 in <i><span class="en">
				D.P.
				937
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔοδμος τῇ ὀσφρήσει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
					<u>HP</u>
					9.13.3
				</span></i>
			: 
				Comp.
			 and 
				Sup.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>CP</u>
				6.16.1
			</span></i>.</div>
